            "title": "Warren Buffett's investing legacy: Consistency is key",
            "description": "<p>Berkshire Hathaway (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-B\">BRK-B</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-A\">BRK-A</a>) CEO Warren Buffett will be stepping down from his chief executive role at the end of 2025. EMJ Capital founder and president Eric Jackson and JonesTrading chief market strategist Michael O'Rourke join Morning Brief with Yahoo Finance Executive Editor <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brian-sozzi/\">Brian Sozzi</a> to discuss what they have learned from Buffett in his 60 years leading Berkshire Hathaway.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/morning-brief/\">Morning Brief</a>.</p>",
